# --- Focus Sync plugin (added 2026-10-09) ---
# The root-level `dist` rule above matches at ANY depth, so it would swallow
# the plugin's hand-maintained runtime payload. Re-include the DIRECTORY
# (not the files inside it): git cannot descend into an excluded directory,
# so negating the files themselves would silently not work.
!extensions/kizemo.focus-sync/dist/
# Build outputs of the plugin, never committed.
extensions/kizemo.focus-sync/bin/
extensions/kizemo.focus-sync/*.exe
# makensis bundles the sidecar from beside installer.nsi, so a copy lands here.
extensions/kizemo.focus-sync/installer/*.exe
# The build publishes its installers here (see scripts/publish-bundle-to-release.mjs),
# so `release/` is a build output and stays untracked.
release/
# Explicit backstop for the built installers. Tauri names them after
# productName, which CONTAINS SPACES: "Alpha File Manager_2.2.0_x64-setup.exe".
# The bare `release/` rule above covers it, but a rule that silently stops
# matching the moment productName changes is exactly the safety net that fails
# when you need it most - so name the real shape explicitly. The legacy Sigma
# spelling is kept while Sigma->Alpha upgrades are still supported.
release/Alpha File Manager_*.exe
release/Sigma File Manager_*.exe
release/Alpha-File-Manager-*.exe

*.tsbuildinfo

flatpak/.deb-input/
flatpak/.build/
flatpak/.repo/
flatpak/output/
